//! task: fix
//! ask: Declare a variable and return it.
//! expect: EXS-E0307
//! refs: §8.6
//! explain: A binding declared without an initializer is not zero-filled, and reading it before any assignment is `EXS-E0307` (definite assignment). Zero-filling would put bytes on the wire that no source line wrote, which is the disclosure class `@transitus` exists to close. Initialise it, with `[0; N]` for an array.

publica functio f() -> u8 {
    mutabilis x: u8;
    redde x;
}
//@ fixed
publica functio f() -> u8 {
    mutabilis x: u8 = 0;
    redde x;
}
